  "prediction": "**Target Impersonation Theft: Fairfax County Police Search for Suspect**\n\nFairfax County police are currently searching for a woman suspected of impersonating a Target employee and stealing over $40,000 worth of iPhones from a store located on Richmond Highway in Alexandria, Virginia. The incident occurred on March 15, when the unidentified woman, dressed as a Target employee, gained access to the stockroom and took the iPhones, placing them in a box before leaving the store.\n\nAccording to police, the suspect was familiar with store procedures, employee hours, and the location of the iPhones in the stockroom, suggesting that she may have had prior knowledge of the store's layout. Surveillance footage shows the woman leaving the store and getting into a Volvo station wagon.\n\nDetectives have released surveillance pictures of the suspect, and anyone with information about the case is encouraged to contact Fairfax County police at 703-691-2131. The suspect is not affiliated with the store, but appeared to have a good understanding of the store's operations.\n\nThe incident highlights the importance of security measures in retail stores, particularly in areas where valuable items are stored. It also serves as a reminder to employees and customers to be vigilant and report any suspicious activity.\n\nThe Fairfax County police are working to identify the suspect and bring her to justice. In the meantime, the community is urged to remain vigilant and report any information that may lead to the capture of the suspect.\n\n**Key Details:**\n\n- Date of incident: March 15\n- Location: Target store on Richmond Highway in Alexandria, Virginia\n- Value of stolen items: Over $40,000 worth of iPhones\n- Suspect description: Unidentified woman dressed as a Target employee\n- Vehicle: Volvo station wagon\n- Contact information: Fairfax County police at 703-691-2131",
